  "keySequence": [
    "MODE",
    "5",
    "4"
  ],
  "summary": "Enter x , y DT pairs (≥2, all x > 0 and y > 0), AC, then recall A, B, and r. Fitted curve: y = A x^B.",
  "body": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Pwr fits y = A x^B — a power law. Use when both variables are positive and a log-log plot would look straight (scaling laws, allometry, intensity vs distance)."
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "plain": "y = A x^{B}"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "mark": "reg-graph",
      "text": "Power regression fits y = A x^B. Both x and y must be positive. B = 1 is proportional; B = 2 is quadratic scaling; fractional B gives slower growth than a straight line."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "mark": "reg-graph",
      "svg": "img/reg/pwr.svg",
      "caption": "Sample fit y = 0.5 x^1.5. A power law looks curved on ordinary axes but becomes a line when both axes are logged."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Input"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Open Pwr regression, clear old data, enter at least two pairs as x , y DT. Every x and y must be greater than zero."
    },
    {
      "type": "keys",
      "keys": [
        "MODE",
        "5",
        "4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "title": "Enter data",
      "items": [
        "SHIFT 9 → 1 EXE if replacing an old list",
        "For each point: x , y DT (x > 0, y > 0)",
        "AC when finished"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "lines",
      "lead": "Example — four points on y = 0.5 x^1.5:",
      "items": [
        "1 , 0.5 DT",
        "2 , 1.41 DT",
        "3 , 2.6 DT",
        "4 , 4 DT",
        "AC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "text": "Minimum 2 pairs. Zero or negative x or y cannot be used in a power fit."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "After AC, recall A (scale factor), B (exponent), and r. The fitted equation is y = A x^B."
    },
    {
      "type": "lines",
      "lead": "S-VAR recalls (after AC):",
      "items": [
        "A — SHIFT 2 → 1 → ▶ → ▶ → 1 EXE",
        "B — SHIFT 2 → 1 → ▶ → ▶ → 2 EXE",
        "r — SHIFT 2 → 1 → ▶ → ▶ → 3 EXE",
        "ŷ for a given x (> 0): type x, SHIFT 2 → 1 → ◀ → 2 EXE",
        "x̂ for a given y (> 0): type y, SHIFT 2 → 1 → ◀ → 1 EXE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Worked example"
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "title": "Points (1, 0.5) and (4, 4)",
      "items": [
        {
          "keys": [
            "MODE",
            "5",
            "4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "SHIFT",
            "9",
            "1",
            "EXE"
          ]
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "1",
            ",",
            "0.5",
            "DT"
          ]
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "4",
            ",",
            "4",
            "DT"
          ]
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "AC"
          ]
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "SHIFT",
            "2",
            "1",
            "▶",
            "▶",
            "1",
            "EXE"
          ],
          "result": "A ≈ 0.5"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "SHIFT",
            "2",
            "1",
            "▶",
            "▶",
            "2",
            "EXE"
          ],
          "result": "B ≈ 1.5"
        },
        {
          "keys": [
            "SHIFT",
            "2",
            "1",
            "▶",
            "▶",
            "3",
            "EXE"
          ],
          "result": "r close to 1"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fitted equation: $y = 0.5 x^{1.5}$"
        },
        {
          "text": "At $x = 2$: $y \\approx 1.41$"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
